{"name":"capture_process_scenario","description":"Run one caller-selected command under a PTY and return process capture Evidence with residual unknowns. Set dry_run: true to validate and return the resolved scenario without launching it; planned Evidence uses the rea.process-scenario-plan predicate and is not a capture. The renderer admits at most 1,000,000 combined terminal cells, computed as columns × (rows + scrollback); every resize uses the selected scrollback and must fit the same budget. Supply a smaller terminal shape when that product is too large; dimensions are never clamped. This release has no runtime override for that cell budget. A command name resolves through the inherited PATH; the working directory defaults to the caller's current directory; host environment variables are inherited with scenario overrides. Environment keys cannot contain '=' or NUL, and REA_PROCESS_RUN_ID is reserved for process ownership. Filesystem snapshots are opt-in through filesystem_observation_paths. A positive finalization_ms makes a timeout or idle deadline send SIGTERM to the captured root through its start identity, keep observing, and send SIGKILL once after the interval; exit.finalization records each attempt with its delivery result and the observed exit, and cancellation still ends the run at once. The target runs with the current user's permissions; this is not a security sandbox.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"arguments":{"items":{"pattern":"^[^\\x00]*$","type":"string"},"type":"array"},"dry_run":{"type":"boolean"},"environment":{"additionalProperties":{"pattern":"^[^\\x00]*$","type":"string"},"propertyNames":{"allOf":[{"pattern":"^(?:[^=\\x00R][^=\\x00]*|R(?:[^=\\x00E][^=\\x00]*|E(?:[^=\\x00A][^=\\x00]*|A(?:[^=\\x00_][^=\\x00]*|_(?:[^=\\x00P][^=\\x00]*|P(?:[^=\\x00R][^=\\x00]*|R(?:[^=\\x00O][^=\\x00]*|O(?:[^=\\x00C][^=\\x00]*|C(?:[^=\\x00E][^=\\x00]*|E(?:[^=\\x00S][^=\\x00]*|S(